#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate TFIM graph {#generate-tfim-graph}"
msgstr "Buat graf TFIM {#generate-tfim-graph}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We begin by defining the lattice of spins and the couplings between them. In"
" this tutorial, the lattice is constructed from connected triangles arranged"
" in a linear chain. Each triangle consists of three nodes connected in a "
"closed loop, and the chain is formed by linking one node of each triangle to"
" the previous triangle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulai dengan mendefinisikan kisi spin dan kopling di antara spin "
"tersebut. Dalam tutorial ini, kisi dibangun dari segitiga-segitiga yang "
"terhubung dan tersusun dalam rantai linier. Setiap segitiga terdiri dari "
"tiga simpul yang terhubung dalam lingkaran tertutup, dan rantai dibentuk "
"dengan menghubungkan satu simpul dari setiap segitiga ke segitiga "
"sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The helper function `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` builds the adjacency "
"matrix for this structure. For a chain of $n$ triangles, the resulting graph"
" contains $2n+1$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi pembantu `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` membangun matriks adjacency"
" untuk struktur ini. Untuk rantai $n$ segitiga, graf yang dihasilkan "
"memiliki $2n+1$ simpul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To visualize the lattice we just defined, we can plot the chain of connected"
" triangles and label each node. The function below builds the graph for a "
"chosen number of triangles and displays it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memvisualisasikan kisi yang baru kita definisikan, kita bisa memplot "
"rantai segitiga yang terhubung dan memberi label pada setiap simpul. Fungsi "
"di bawah ini membangun graf untuk jumlah segitiga yang dipilih dan "
"menampilkannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this tutorial we will use a chain of 20 triangles.\n"
msgstr "Untuk tutorial ini kita akan menggunakan rantai 20 segitiga.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Coloring graph edges {#coloring-graph-edges}"
msgstr "Pewarnaan sisi graf {#coloring-graph-edges}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the spin–spin coupling, it is useful to group edges that do not"
" overlap. This allows us to apply two-qubit gates in parallel. We can do "
"this with a simple edge-coloring procedure [\\[1\\]](#references), which "
"assigns a color to each edge so that edges meeting at the same node are "
"placed in different groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengimplementasikan kopling spin–spin, sangat berguna untuk "
"mengelompokkan sisi-sisi yang tidak tumpang tindih. Ini memungkinkan kita "
"menerapkan gate dua qubit secara paralel. Kita bisa melakukannya dengan "
"prosedur pewarnaan sisi sederhana [\\[1\\]](#references), yang memberikan "
"warna pada setiap sisi sehingga sisi-sisi yang bertemu di simpul yang sama "
"ditempatkan dalam kelompok berbeda.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi pada perangkat keras kuantum "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate Trotterized circuits on spin graphs {#generate-trotterized-"
"circuits-on-spin-graphs}"
msgstr ""
"Hasilkan Circuit Trotter pada graf spin {#generate-trotterized-circuits-on-"
"spin-graphs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate the dynamics of the TFIM, we construct circuits that approximate"
" the time evolution operator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mensimulasikan dinamika TFIM, kita membangun Circuit yang "
"mengaproksimasi operator evolusi waktu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We use a second-order Trotter decomposition:\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan dekomposisi Trotter orde kedua:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ and $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i"
" Z_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ dan $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} "
"Z_i Z_j$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The $H_X$ term is implemented with layers of `RX` rotations.\n"
msgstr "Suku $H_X$ diimplementasikan dengan lapisan rotasi `RX`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $H_Z$ term is implemented with layers of `RZZ` gates along the edges of "
"the interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suku $H_Z$ diimplementasikan dengan lapisan Gate `RZZ` sepanjang sisi-sisi "
"graf interaksi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angles of these gates are determined by the transverse field $h$, the "
"coupling constant $J$, and the time step $\\Delta t$. By stacking multiple "
"Trotter steps, we generate circuits of increasing depth that approximate the"
" system's dynamics. The functions `generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` and "
"`trotter_circuits` construct a Trotterized quantum circuit from an arbitrary"
" spin interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut-sudut Gate ini ditentukan oleh medan transversal $h$, konstanta "
"kopling $J$, dan langkah waktu $\\Delta t$. Dengan menumpuk beberapa langkah"
" Trotter, kita menghasilkan Circuit dengan kedalaman yang semakin bertambah "
"untuk mengaproksimasi dinamika sistem. Fungsi "
"`generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` dan `trotter_circuits` membangun Circuit "
"kuantum Trotter dari graf interaksi spin sembarang.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimate single-qubit magnetizations $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-"
"single-qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"
msgstr ""
"Estimasi magnetisasi single-Qubit $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-single-"
"qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To study the dynamics of the model, we want to measure the magnetization of "
"each qubit, defined by the expectation value $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = "
"\\langle \\psi | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mempelajari dinamika model, kita ingin mengukur magnetisasi setiap "
"qubit, yang didefinisikan oleh nilai ekspektasi $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = "
"\\langle \\psi | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simulations, we can compute this directly from the measurement outcomes. "
"The function `z_expectation` processes the bitstring counts and returns the "
"value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for a chosen qubit index. On real hardware,"
" we evaluate the same quantity by specifying the Pauli operator using the "
"function `generate_z_observables`, and then the backend computes the "
"expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam simulasi, kita bisa menghitungnya langsung dari hasil pengukuran. "
"Fungsi `z_expectation` memproses jumlah bitstring dan mengembalikan nilai "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ untuk indeks qubit yang dipilih. Pada perangkat "
"keras nyata, kita mengevaluasi kuantitas yang sama dengan menentukan "
"operator Pauli menggunakan fungsi `generate_z_observables`, lalu Backend "
"akan menghitung nilai ekspektasinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now define the parameters for generating the Trotterized circuits. In "
"this tutorial, the lattice is a chain of 20 connected triangles, which "
"corresponds to a 41-qubit system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita mendefinisikan parameter untuk menghasilkan Circuit Trotter. "
"Dalam tutorial ini, kisi adalah rantai 20 segitiga terhubung, yang sesuai "
"dengan sistem 41-Qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"
msgstr "Jalankan simulasi MPS {#run-mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The list of Trotterized circuits is executed using the "
"`matrix_product_state` simulator with an arbitrary choice of $4096$ shots. "
"The MPS method provides an efficient approximation of the circuit dynamics, "
"with accuracy determined by the chosen bond dimension. For the system sizes "
"considered here, the default bond dimension is sufficient to capture the "
"magnetization dynamics with high fidelity. The raw counts are normalized, "
"and from these we compute the single-qubit expectation values $\\langle Z_i "
"\\rangle$ at each Trotter step. Finally, we calculate the average over all "
"qubits to obtain a single curve that shows how the magnetization changes "
"over time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Daftar Circuit Trotter dieksekusi menggunakan simulator "
"`matrix_product_state` dengan pilihan arbitrer $4096$ shot. Metode MPS "
"memberikan aproksimasi efisien dari dinamika Circuit, dengan akurasi yang "
"ditentukan oleh dimensi ikatan yang dipilih. Untuk ukuran sistem yang "
"dipertimbangkan di sini, dimensi ikatan default sudah cukup untuk menangkap "
"dinamika magnetisasi dengan fidelitas tinggi. Jumlah mentah dinormalisasi, "
"dan dari sini kita menghitung nilai ekspektasi single-Qubit $\\langle Z_i "
"\\rangle$ pada setiap langkah Trotter. Akhirnya, kita menghitung rata-rata "
"atas semua qubit untuk mendapatkan satu kurva yang menunjukkan bagaimana "
"magnetisasi berubah seiring waktu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Jalankan pada perangkat keras {#run-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan pada perangkat keras dengan Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-"
"opal}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We evaluate the magnetization dynamics on real quantum hardware. Fire Opal "
"provides a Qiskit Function that extends the standard Qiskit Runtime "
"Estimator primitive with automated error suppression and performance "
"management. We submit the Trotterized circuits directly to an IBM&reg; "
"backend while Fire Opal handles the noise-aware execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengevaluasi dinamika magnetisasi pada perangkat keras kuantum nyata. "
"Fire Opal menyediakan Qiskit Function yang memperluas primitif Estimator "
"Qiskit Runtime standar dengan penekanan kesalahan otomatis dan manajemen "
"performa. Kita mengirimkan Circuit Trotter langsung ke Backend IBM&reg; "
"sementara Fire Opal menangani eksekusi yang peka terhadap noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We prepare a list of `pubs`, where each item contains a circuit and the "
"corresponding Pauli-Z observables. These are passed to Fire Opal's estimator"
" function, which returns the expectation values $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for "
"each qubit at each Trotter step. The results can then be averaged over "
"qubits to obtain the magnetization curve from hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menyiapkan daftar `pubs`, di mana setiap item berisi sebuah sirkuit dan"
" observable Pauli-Z yang sesuai. Ini diteruskan ke fungsi estimator Fire "
"Opal, yang mengembalikan nilai ekspektasi $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ untuk "
"setiap qubit pada setiap langkah Trotter. Hasilnya kemudian bisa dirata-"
"ratakan atas semua qubit untuk mendapatkan kurva magnetisasi dari perangkat "
"keras.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang "
"diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-"
"format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we compare the magnetization curve from the simulator with the "
"results obtained on real hardware. Plotting both side by side shows how "
"closely the hardware execution with Fire Opal matches the noiseless baseline"
" across Trotter steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, kita membandingkan kurva magnetisasi dari simulator dengan hasil "
"yang diperoleh pada perangkat keras nyata. Memplot keduanya secara "
"berdampingan menunjukkan seberapa dekat eksekusi perangkat keras dengan Fire"
" Opal cocok dengan baseline tanpa noise di seluruh langkah Trotter.\n"

